{
 "nodes": [
  {
   "id": "cap-btitle",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -700,
   "y": -330,
   "width": 1500,
   "height": 150,
   "text": "# Gemma 4 31B-it — one decoder layer (sliding, 50 of 60: 479.0M)  \nGrey bars = tensors (0.05 px/channel), boxes = operations with their weights. Sandwich norms: each sub-block is wrapped by an RMSNorm before *and* after, then added to the residual; the layer output is scaled by a learned scalar."
  },
  {
   "id": "cap-blegend",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 900,
   "y": -330,
   "width": 1300,
   "height": 150,
   "text": "Sliding layers: causal window 1024, GQA 32/16 × 256, RoPE θ 10,000 on all 256 dims.    \nThe 10 full layers (every 6th, 534.0M) differ only in attention — see the panel on the right. Norms, residuals and the MLP are identical."
  },
  {
   "id": "xin1",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -134,
   "y": 0,
   "width": 269,
   "height": 9,
   "text": "",
   "color": "#64748b"
  },
  {
   "id": "note-lbl2",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 170,
   "y": -10,
   "width": 440,
   "height": 34,
   "text": "`x [T, 5376]  residual stream in`"
  },
  {
