  },
  {
   "id": "note-lbl48",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 170,
   "y": 2332,
   "width": 440,
   "height": 34,
   "text": "`x [T, 5376]  → next layer`"
  },
  {
   "id": "note-qk",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -1100,
   "y": 444,
   "width": 420,
   "height": 190,
   "text": "**q/k norm** — RMSNorm with a learned 256-wide weight on every head; v gets a weightless RMSNorm. Because q and k are normalised, the attention scale is 1 instead of 1/√256. KV cache per token: 8,192 values (K+V, 16 heads × 256), kept for the last 1024 tokens."
  },
  {
   "id": "note-norm",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -1100,
   "y": 1086,
   "width": 420,
   "height": 120,
   "text": "All four layer norms are RMSNorm × w (plain weight, not 1 + w). MLP is GeGLU: gelu_pytorch_tanh(gate) × up, 346.8M per layer."
  },
  {
   "id": "cap-full",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 2200,
   "y": 184,
   "width": 1300,
   "height": 110,
   "text": "**Full-attention layers** (L5, L11, L17 … L59) — attention only; the rest of the layer is the same. 4 wide KV heads, and **K = V**: there is no v_proj."
  },
  {
   "id": "fq49",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 2250,
   "y": 444,
   "width": 300,
   "height": 56,
   "text": "**q_proj** 5376 → 16384  \n88.1M",
   "color": "5"
  },
  {
   "id": "fqt50",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 2200,
   "y": 540,
   "width": 400,
   "height": 9,
   "text": "",
